(XI)--निर्गुण and apart from प्रकृति: makes his devotees the poorest so as to create in them a spirit of detachment: Blesses and curses: In the garb of a Brahma- चारिन् persuaded वृक to test शिव's boon on himself: भृगु kicked the sleeping Hari in his chest and helped him to get united with लक्ष्मी: भृगु's wonder at it;
1: भा. X. Chh. ८८-89.
Has root in religious performances of Brahmanas and is himself यज्ञ and source of all Dharma: the २५थ् principle: Helped शिव in regaining his lost glory through Maya: took the form of a cow and with ब्रह्मा as calf drank the immortalising fluid of the well in Tripura;
2: Ib.

